=== Hybrid Signature Structure ===

Hybrid signatures combine:
  - Ed25519: Classical elliptic curve signature
  - ML-DSA-65: Post-quantum lattice-based signature

Sizes:
  Public key:  1984 bytes (32 + 1952)
  Secret key:  4096 bytes (64 + 4032)
  Signature:   3373 bytes (64 + 3309)

Signing Flow:
  1. sig1 = Ed25519.Sign(sk1, message)
  2. sig2 = ML-DSA.Sign(sk2, message)
  3. hybrid_sig = sig1 || sig2

Verification Flow:
  1. Verify Ed25519 signature
  2. Verify ML-DSA signature
  3. Accept only if BOTH verify

Security: Secure if EITHER Ed25519 OR ML-DSA is secure
  - Classical attackers cannot forge Ed25519
  - Quantum attackers cannot forge ML-DSA

All tests passed!
